{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:27Z","created_by_operation":"op_177575d15fca43ad8a67b42c36670c89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c3b729945ed711ee85cd235743e325bd06bb55af181f7279ab969c0fb5c7c5b9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"primeintellect-ai/prime-agent@1fc1adb6e806 snapshot 500e7d550bac7429","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4d1559e14ff8dfe23b95576419ebc6aa65f3593be64ef0d9bea0635f85ef7a9c"],"source_ids":["src_7305b7512bc25bbaa92b5721bc981ef2"],"text":"The agent and TUI are built on top of the open-source 'pi' project, which the README acknowledges.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:27Z","updated_by_operation":"op_177575d15fca43ad8a67b42c36670c89"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:27Z","created_by_operation":"op_177575d15fca43ad8a67b42c36670c89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e1b89d0f1bd9fb8c0bf46d8ca9695479f2bd9250246977494ab184f583b2cd33","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"primeintellect-ai/prime-agent@1fc1adb6e806 snapshot 500e7d550bac7429","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1ac130da41e40724ad9cf590ea283e2e92a2c5c053faba11e4009b0bc13a1290","slc_8e191a5d86ed2ab000eb3ef1838bc79830883c4dc70e2c271f565a31d71310b4"],"source_ids":["src_7305b7512bc25bbaa92b5721bc981ef2"],"text":"Prime Agent is built around two abstractions: a Recursive Language Model that treats context as variables and subagents as function calls in a persistent REPL, and a Continual Harness storing prompts, memories, skills, and subagent specs as durable state.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:27Z","updated_by_operation":"op_177575d15fca43ad8a67b42c36670c89"}
